    "text": "Ic Agatho papa of Rome grete wel seo wur\u00f0fulle \u00e6\u00f0elred Myrcene kyning & se \u00e6rcebiscop Theodorum\n& seo Myrcene biscop Saxulf seo \u00e6r w\u00e6s abbot.\n& alle \u00fea abbotes \u00fea sindon on Englalande Godes gretinge & minre bletsunge.\nIc haue geheord seo kyninges \u00e6\u00f0elredes geornunge & \u00fees \u00e6rcebiscopes Theodorus, & \u00fees biscopes\nAnd ic bebeode of Godes half & Sancte Petres, & ealra halgan, & ealre hadode heafde, \u00feet ne kyning ne\nIc beode \u00e6c \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fee scyrbiscop ne seo swa dyrstlece \u00fe\u00e6t he na hading ne haleging ne do on \u00feis abbotrice\n& ic wille \u00fe\u00e6t seo abbot beo gehealden for legat of Rome ofer eal \u00fe\u00e6t iglande, & hwilc abbot \u00fee be\u00fe\nIc wille & ty\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t whilc man swa haued behaten to faren to Rome, and he ne muge hit for\u00f0ian, ou\u00f0er\n& haue \u00fe\u00e6t ilce forgiuenesse of Criste & Sancte Peter, & of \u00feonne abbot & of \u00feone muneca \u00fe\u00e6t he\nNu bidde ic \u00fee bro\u00f0er Theodorus \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu lete bedon geond \u00e6l Englelande \u00feet seo sina\u00f0 wur\u00f0e\nAl swa ic beode \u00fee Saxulf biscop \u00fe\u00e6t swa swa \u00feu hit geornest, \u00fe\u00e6t seo mynstre beo freo, swa ic\nNu wille ic hit segge mid worde \u00fe\u00e6t hwa swa halt \u00feis write & \u00feis bode.\n\u00dea wur\u00f0e he efre wuniende mid God \u00e6lmihti on heuenrice, & hwa swa hit to brece\u00f0, \u00fea wur\u00f0e he\n\u00d0as writ seonde seo papa Agatho & an hundred & fif & twenti biscopes bi Wilfrid \u00e6rcebiscop of\n\u00deis w\u00e6s gedon \u00e6fter ure Drihtnes acennednesse dclxxx \u00fees kininges vi gear \u00e6\u00f0elredes.\n\u00d0a heot seo kining \u00feone \u00e6rcebiscop Theodorus \u00fe\u00e6t he scolde setton ealle gewitenemot \u00e6t \u00feone stede\n\u00d0a hi w\u00e6ron \u00fe\u00e6r gegaderod, \u00fea leot he r\u00e6don \u00fea gewrite \u00fee seo papa \u00feider seonde, & ealle hit getton &\n\u00d0a seide se kyning, Ealle \u00fea \u00feing \u00fee min bro\u00f0er Peada, & min bro\u00f0er Wulfere, & mine swuster\n& ic wile on min d\u00e6i hit \u00e6con for here sawle, & for minre sawle.\nNu gife ic Sancte Peter to d\u00e6i in to his minstre Medeshamstede \u00feas landes, & eal \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r to ligge\u00f0, \u00feet\n\u00d0as landes ic gife Sancte Peter eal swa freolice swa ic seolf hit ahte, & swa \u00fe\u00e6t nan min \u00e6ftergengles\nGif hwa hit do\u00f0, \u00fees papa curs of Rome & ealre biscope curs he habbe, & here ealre \u00fee her be\n& \u00feis ic festnie mid Cristes tacne.\nIc Theodorus \u00e6rcebiscop of Cantwarbyrig am witnesse of \u00feas gewrite of Medeshamstede, & ic festnie\nIc Wilfrid \u00e6rcebiscop of \u00e6ferwic ic eam witnesse of \u00feas gewrite, & ic g\u00e6te \u00fe\u00e6s ilce curs.\nIc Saxulf \u00fee w\u00e6s first abbot & nu eam biscop ic gife hi min curs & ealle min \u00e6ftergengle \u00fee \u00feis\nIc Ostri\u00f0e \u00e6\u00f0elredes cwen hit ty\u00f0e.\nIc Adrianus legat hit iete.\nIc Putta biscop of Rofecestre ic hit write.\nIc Waldhere biscop of Lundene hit festnie.\nIc Cu\u00f0bald abbot hit geate swa \u00feet hwa swa hit breket.\nEalre biscope cursunge & eal Cristene foces he hafe, Amen.",
